    "title": "Empire State Building Goes Gold for Voyager",
    "url": "https://www.nasa.gov/image-article/empire-state-building-goes-gold-for-voyager/",
    "text": "NASA/Bill Ingalls The Empire State Building is seen illuminated in gold to celebrate NASA s Voyager 1 spacecraft as it was about to pass one light-day away from Earth, a distance reached by no other human-made object, Nov. 17, 2026. The color gold represents the gold-plated copper phonograph record that is flying on Voyager; the Golden Record contains sounds and images selected to portray the diversity of life and culture on Earth. Image credit: NASA/Bill Ingalls",
